# Hand-written from the sources: the types and callables each file declares,
# as `class|function <name>@<path relative to this directory>`. Variables,
# fields and the synthetic <script> entry are not part of the contract.
# A Jenkinsfile and a build.gradle declare nothing of their own.
class Kube@src/org/acme/Kube.groovy
function Kube@src/org/acme/Kube.groovy
function apply@src/org/acme/Kube.groovy
function rollback@src/org/acme/Kube.groovy
function call@vars/deploy.groovy
function call@vars/notify.groovy
function failed@vars/notify.groovy

# Declared reader limits. Kube.groovy has an untyped field (`def steps`) and
# an untyped constructor parameter; the Java-shaped Groovy grammar parses
# that pair with ERROR nodes, so the constructor is lost and the field is read
# as a function. `!missing` is declared above but not produced; `!spurious` is
# produced but not declared. The test requires both to hold exactly: the day
# the reader gets it right, this block must go.
!missing function Kube@src/org/acme/Kube.groovy
!spurious function steps@src/org/acme/Kube.groovy
